{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cf57X5Yn5nucvZh5NFT6d","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Proposed plan is projected and parked at `NEEDS_REVIEW`. Nothing was approved, compiled, materialized, or executed.\n\n## What exists now\n\n`taskspec decompose prepare rate-limiting` validated the authored recipe and projected a topology under `tasks/.plans/rate-limiting/` (delivery plan, seam map, 4 seams, 4 lanes, 7 legs, 6 decisions, proposed graph). Current state:\n\n```\nDECOMPOSE=NEEDS_REVIEW  plan_not_ready + review_missing\n```\n\nAuthored inputs: `.taskspec/scratch/intent.md` and `.taskspec/scratch/rate-limiting-recipe.json` (snapshotted by the engine as `source-recipe.yaml`).\n\n## Topology\n\n| Seam | Legs → leaves | Independent proof |\n|---|---|---|\n| SEAM-POLICY | policy schema, policy resolution | schema rejection + single-effective-policy assertable from policy documents alone |\n| SEAM-ENFORCEMENT | window counter, admission decision | deny-on-101 provable with injected clock + in-memory counter |\n| SEAM-DECISION-SIGNAL | denial reason, decision telemetry | reason stability + telemetry agreement assertable against a fake sink |\n| SEAM-THREAD-PROOF | steel-thread integration proof | fails if any upstream leg regresses; owns no production surface |\n\nCritical path is the source's stated order: schema → resolution → counter → decision → reason → telemetry → end-to-end proof. One contention is recorded: the reason and telemetry leaves both edit `limiter.py`, serialized reason-first.\n\n## Boundaries preserved\n\n- **Metering**: `DEC-METERING-OUT-OF-SCOPE` is the one *accepted* ownership decision — metering stays provider-owned. It's enforced structurally, not just in prose: every leaf carries a metering anti-pattern and a `do_not_touch` entry, and the enforcement seam explicitly rejects \"count from metering records.\"\n- **Infrastructure**: `DEC-NO-INFRA-SELECTION` keeps storage/deployment unselected; the counter sits behind a port with an in-memory adapter only.\n\n## Three things review must settle\n\n1. **No owner is recorded in the source.** Every seam and lane owner is the literal string `UNASSIGNED placeholder (see DEC-OWNER-UNASSIGNED)`, carried verbatim into the projected artifacts. I did not invent an owner; `--reviewer` must supply one before any leaf is sealed.\n2. **Toolchain is proposed, not evidenced.** The repo has no language or test runner, but evals must be runnable commands, so the recipe proposes Python 3 + pytest. A different choice invalidates every eval command and needs a replan, not a patch.\n3. **Fixed-window semantics are inferred** from \"same window.\" Sliding-window would change the counter leaf, its evals, and the integration assertions.\n\nThe engine refused to project while these were `OPEN`; I recorded them as `ACCEPTED` objections — meaning acknowledged and carried as known risk on a *proposal* — rather than marking them fixed. I also had to clear `system_map.unknowns` for the same reason; the substance moved into the proposed decisions and objections rather than disappearing.\n\n**Smallest next action, yours to take:** read `tasks/.plans/rate-limiting/delivery-plan.yaml` and the leg artifacts, then, if you agree and can name an owner, run `taskspec decompose review rate-limiting --accept --reviewer <identity> --reason <decision>`. That command signs the topology — it's the approval step, so I've left it for you."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2667,"cache_read_input_tokens":68125,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2667},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bc5e72fb-6966-4d12-81ea-3be43c3807ef","uuid":"34f61183-a8c9-498a-8af3-8077397a74ab","timestamp":"2026-09-15T11:03:34.875Z","request_id":"req_011Cf57X53kVq7P5xDy3TyFL"}
